From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:17:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Keep MediaQueryLists with change listeners alive

The window only held its MediaQueryLists weakly, so a list that the page
no longer referenced was collected with its listeners, and later changes
were not reported. Chromium and Gecko keep such lists alive while they
have change listeners; do the same.

Fork note: meant for upstream; found with the QuickJS backend, but
SpiderMonkey loses the listeners too once a GC runs in between (the new
test times out without this change). Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: Adds a WPT test that times out without this change.

Validation: Release builds of this stack (QuickJS through the QuickJS workflow's patch step, servo-quickjs 0605066) with `./mach test-wpt --processes 4` of html/webappapis/microtask-queuing, user-timing and /_mozilla/mozilla/media-query-list-gc-listener.html (72 tests): all as expected with QuickJS; with SpiderMonkey all as expected except an unexpected PASS of a subtest of measure_associated_with_navigation_timing.html that compares a sum of measure durations, without measure options.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; root-caused, written and tested by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 components/script/dom/event/eventtarget.rs    |  6 ++++++
 components/script/dom/media/mediaquerylist.rs |  5 +++++
 components/script/dom/window/window.rs        | 18 ++++++++++++++++
 tests/wpt/mozilla/meta/MANIFEST.json          |  7 +++++++
 .../mozilla/media-query-list-gc-listener.html | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
